<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi British Bank nine-month net rises.</title>
<headline>Saudi British Bank nine-month net rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(billion riyals unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		  359.9 million    vs  304.2 million</p>
<p> Operating income	    1.41	     vs    1.33</p>
<p> Operating expenses	  1.06	     vs    1.04</p>
<p> Other income		 13.8 million    vs   14.8 million</p>
<p> Provision		    50.7 million    vs   35.3 million</p>
<p> Net loans and advances    9.57	     vs    9.61</p>
<p> Investment securities    13.96	     vs   10.73</p>
<p> Shareholders' fund	  3.04	     vs    2.89</p>
<p> Total assets		 30.62	     vs   25.78</p>
<p>Full Name: The Saudi British Bank.</p>
<p>Note - The Riyadh-based bank is 40 percent owned by HSBC Holding Plc, the parent of Hong Kong and Shanghai Corp. The rest is held by Saudi Arabian investors.</p>
</text>
